      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Edges & gradients playground\n\nGreen Row: The same denoised grayscale through the classic edge operators. Sobel d/dx and d/dy (float, signed!) fed to cartToPolar; the magnitude is previewed normalized, and the DIRECTION goes through 'CV Flow To Color' - the color-wheel render (hue = angle, brightness = magnitude) that optical-flow papers use; flat areas come out black because nothing points anywhere.\n\nBlue Row: The same steps as the green row but the gradients are obtained via cv2.spatialGradient.\n\nBottom row: Compare with the Laplacian (zero-crossings, no direction) and Canny (thresholded + thinned + hysteresis - already a decision, not a gradient)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
